  "content": {
    "id": "p59-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Solve for $\\theta\\in[0^{\\circ},360^{\\circ})$. Remember to take positive and negative values when square rooting.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p59-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin^2\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=90^{\\circ},\\ 270^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=\\pm\\sqrt{1}\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\pm1\\end{align*}$$\nThese values occur on the vertical axis of the unit circle.\n$$\\theta=90^{\\circ},\\ 270^{\\circ}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p59-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2\\theta=\\dfrac34$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ},\\ 210^{\\circ},\\ 330^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac34}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\A&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)\\\\A&=30^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nBoth signs are included, so use all four quadrants.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=30^{\\circ},\\ 180^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ},\\\\&\\phantom{=}180^{\\circ}+30^{\\circ},\\ 360^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ},\\ 210^{\\circ},\\ 330^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p59-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan^2\\theta=3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=60^{\\circ},\\ 120^{\\circ},\\ 240^{\\circ},\\ 300^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\pm\\sqrt3\\\\A&=\\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt3)\\\\A&=60^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nBoth signs are included, so use all four quadrants.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=60^{\\circ},\\ 180^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ},\\\\&\\phantom{=}180^{\\circ}+60^{\\circ},\\ 360^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=60^{\\circ},\\ 120^{\\circ},\\ 240^{\\circ},\\ 300^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      }
    ]
  },
